{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type","id":1492313,"title":"Homesteads (freehold type)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-04T13:55:57-07:00","id":1492313,"title":"Homesteads (freehold type)","content":"Freeholds are usually defined by their function of serving a gateway between the Autumn World and the Dreaming. But one type are homesteads which exist solely in the Dreaming. Instead of serving as a door between worlds, they provide local stability to anchor the local Dreaming into a stable form.<br /> <br /> Now Changelings who inhabit such a homestead are likely to live most of their time far more in the Dreaming than the Autumn World. But they are still Changelings and still need to spend some time there so not to succumb to Bedlam. Given they likely spend around the minimum time required for that, they would have the fewest ties to mortal. They probably don't have steady jobs, places of residence, and other things that require an ongoing presence in the Autumn World. At the same time, I do think they could have sufficient ties to mortals and mortal society to stave off Bedlam especially if they are supported by some Changelings who do have resources in the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> Some sort of vagrant concept would work, but not necessarily be someone who is homeless. They could be various kind of seasonal workers, visiting relatives, criminals, carnies, migrant workers and such. Since mortal attachments are important to avoid Bedlam, it'd be best if such Changelings could run into the same people year after year despite being gone for extended periods.<br /> <br /> I also imagine that any Siochain might prefer to stay in homesteads since it should provide less challenges to them than it does to others.<br /> <br /> Wondering how extensive people have used homesteads in their own chronicles, and how you've dealt with the practicalities of running such freeholds.<br /> <br /> I like homesteads because they can expand the Dreaming and give more depth to that aspect of the chronicle. But it seems to me to provide some challenges to make the concept work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T14:09:25-07:00","id":1492315,"title":"","content":"One freehold type might be a tourist attraction. Someplace where banality was low and glamour might be had from those in the right mode. Think about a Mystery Shack like the one in Gravity Falls (which was based on thousands of similar attractions). Picture it in an isolated microclimate between a desert and the mountain forests. Not odd in the Southwest. Exhibits, a gift shop, a restaurant (probably run by Bogguns with a Nocker chef). Perhaps Kithian and Nunnehine run the place together. Maybe it could be a small amusement park with an Old West theme. <br /> <br /> The isolation would preserve the freehold, while the tourists brought in glamour. The Changelings would have a place to live, and steady jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T20:33:37-07:00","id":1492335,"title":"","content":"I don't think the keepers of a Homestead would be of a vagrant concept. After all, they do have a stable residence: the Homestead itself. And most of them, being in the Near Dreaming or having Silver Paths to known Freeholds, are somewhat tied to specific places. I think those types would resemble more people that live in neighboring cities, towns or farms, the kind that visits sometimes but spend most of it at their own place (and can claim to live in a known village or something, this might be even true).<br /> <br /> Homesteads are also likely to have the means to facilitate this to their permanent inhabitants. The Freeholder may have land near to one Trod that leads there and let them claim to live there, maybe even have actual homes there for their staying in the Autumn World. It may grow some chimerical produce they exchange with other Freeholds and from this get either the resources or the excuse to the wandering in the Autumn World. Hence any permanent inhabitant will need to go to the Autumn World with some frequency anyway, the Homestead is likely organized with that in mind.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify something: C20 finally gave rules for Bedlam, and from that we got a hard number: a Changeling accrues 1 Nightmare every full week in the Dreaming. 10 Nightmare become 1 Imbalance that applies to a WP dot, if all WP dots get Imbalances, you get into full Bedlam and is just a matter of time before you're completely Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T21:40:52-07:00","id":1492341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492335#post1492335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the keepers of a Homestead would be of a vagrant concept. After all, they do have a stable residence: the Homestead itself. And most of them, being in the Near Dreaming or having Silver Paths to known Freeholds, are somewhat tied to specific places. I think those types would resemble more people that live in neighboring cities, towns or farms, the kind that visits sometimes but spend most of it at their own place (and can claim to live in a known village or something, this might be even true).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, while in the Dreaming itself, the homesteaders would have a permanent residence and do whatever things they would normally do to make a living in the Dreaming (Boggans farming, Nockers mining, Satyrs tending livestock, etc.). By vagrant, I meant their mortal seemings. Because most of their time is spent in the Dreaming, and they don't have instant access to the Autumn World (they would need to travel to find another freehold to crossover into the Autumn World), I don't think they could have normal mortal occupations, and thus would need to survive by alternate means of work (seasonal jobs, itinerant work, temp jobs, etc.) and wouldn't have permanent housing because rent and mortgage obligations would be difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492335#post1492335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homesteads are also likely to have the means to facilitate this to their permanent inhabitants. The Freeholder may have land near to one Trod that leads there and let them claim to live there, maybe even have actual homes there for their staying in the Autumn World. It may grow some chimerical produce they exchange with other Freeholds and from this get either the resources or the excuse to the wandering in the Autumn World. Hence any permanent inhabitant will need to go to the Autumn World with some frequency anyway, the Homestead is likely organized with that in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they definitely should be organized in such a way that homesteaders can still travel to the Autumn World and do whatever is necessary to retain enough mortal ties to avoid Bedlam. I'm just looking for examples of how people may have actually done this in their chronicles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492335#post1492335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify something: C20 finally gave rules for Bedlam, and from that we got a hard number: a Changeling accrues 1 Nightmare every full week in the Dreaming. 10 Nightmare become 1 Imbalance that applies to a WP dot, if all WP dots get Imbalances, you get into full Bedlam and is just a matter of time before you're completely Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad system to provide more guidance to STs. I am curious, is there any way to remove Nightmare levels so balance can be achieved? I would assume that every full week in the Autumn World might remove it. But since I don't own C20, that assumption could easily be wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T04:33:05-07:00","id":1492357,"title":"","content":"My point is that their mortal seemings would be more probably the rural sort instead of the vagrant. Work in the family farm, or other family business, comes to the city from time to time to trade with the family clients (other Freeholds), so that's why they don't live nearby but come from time to time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492341#post1492341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a bad system to provide more guidance to STs. I am curious, is there any way to remove Nightmare levels so balance can be achieved? I would assume that every full week in the Autumn World might remove it. But since I don't own C20, that assumption could easily be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are, but removing is harder than gaining them. You need quite some dedicated time to mortal life to remove Imbalance. At the end of the day, avoiding getting Nightmare too frequently is the best option, so in a Homestead things would be organized so everyone has at least a weekly forage into the Autumn World (which some may miss).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T11:09:16-07:00","id":1492376,"title":"","content":"The Homestead would need a cover, a family farm would be a possibility. <br /> <br /> Another might be an old hippie commune that makes something that is sold in quaint little shops. Goat's Milk Soap, genuine beeswax candles, New Agey quilts, etc. Odd behavior from leftover Hippies and their kids would go unnoticed. <br /> <br /> A New Age consciousness Center, one of those places people go to for retreats that involve aroma therapy, massage, yoga, and other things New Agey. Again, who'd notice weird behavior from a place like that?<br /> <br /> My earlier idea of a tourist attraction. <br /> <br /> A dinner theater. These are normally urban but in an area with a steady flow of tourists they could be in a semi rural area. Again, strange behavior would be expected, and thus go unnoticed. <br /> <br /> Each of these gives the Homestead Freehold an income and sources of glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T19:54:32-07:00","id":1492407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492376#post1492376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homestead would need a cover</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they explored Homesteads in C20, but no, it doesn't need a cover.<br /> <br /> The point of the Homestead is that it exists solely on the Dreaming. It is not a Freehold in the usual sense of a place of respite against the Autumn World, it offers respite against the ever-changing nature of the Dreaming. It doesn't even need to be in the Near Dreaming, some are located in the Far Dreaming (and theoretically there could be some in the Deep Dreaming).<br /> <br /> So the point is that it doesn't have any counterpoint in the Autumn World. It's its denizens that need an explanation to be away from town most of the time, completely unreachable to their human acquaintances, yet they come back from time to time. How to explain where you have been when the place you have been doesn't exist in this world whatsoever?<br /> <br /> Likewise, Homesteads have no <i>direct</i> links to the Autumn World. They may have trods to there, but not a direct entrance, and even those aren't common. Most Homesteads require a journey through several trods to reach a Freehold in the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> Changeling has one big problem in that most pre-20 supplements have a visible problem of leaning so much in one aspect of the game the author liked as to effectively ignore and contradict lore of other aspects, at least to a degree. Most of the time it isn't a big problem, but it does means some inconsistencies have to be accounted for to understand a given element of the supplements. Homesteads fit this bill. Their original depiction completely ignores that Changelings aren't the original state of the Kithain and that Bedlam exists for them, so they work as Dreaming Freeholds that were cut from the Autumn World during the Interregnum and now conflict ensues, and their inhabitants are completely normal Changelings just 'cause.<br /> <br /> You take from that what you want and adapt, as unfortunately must be done with too many supplements for the game. I'd say it has one of the most solid core books pre-<i>Revised</i> (it never got an actual <i>Revised</i> edition) in both editions, but the supplements are way out of pace with the cores. I'm still working some of my own conclusions, but I personally like in V20 to use the rules for Dark-Kin, with a few tweaks, to represent the eventual non-Changeling Kithain that still lives within the Dreaming, like most of House Danaan in V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T21:16:45-07:00","id":1492410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492357#post1492357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that their mortal seemings would be more probably the rural sort instead of the vagrant. Work in the family farm, or other family business, comes to the city from time to time to trade with the family clients (other Freeholds), so that's why they don't live nearby but come from time to time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a family farm working because running even a small farm takes a lot of time that the Changelings of a homestead just don't have. Any such farm would have to be run by humans, and unless those humans are knowing Kinain or somehow permanently enchanted, I don't see why they'd accommodate some person who just arrives. Even if it is a family member that host the Changeling, families just aren't going to accept someone running off and being away way most of the time. Family run businesses require family members to be dependable workers in whatever capacity they have. Children of course can work less because of other commitments like school, but the overall mortal responsibilities don't match the limited time Changeling homesteaders can devote to the mortal world.<br /> <br /> Of course, farms can use some seasonal workers around harvest time, but that places them in the migrating/seasonal workers mode again. That could earn them some money, keep some mortal ties if they keep coming back again, and so on. It can definitely work, but that's already along the lines I am thinking, and I don't think that's what you mean by involving family businesses.<br /> <br /> If you mean such families are basically Kinain who knowingly serve Changelings and allow them access whenever needed, then yeah, that could work. But that's not how I see most Kinain. But I guess it would be an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T21:31:03-07:00","id":1492412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492376#post1492376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A New Age consciousness Center, one of those places people go to for retreats that involve aroma therapy, massage, yoga, and other things New Agey. Again, who'd notice weird behavior from a place like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about places where weird behavior would be accepted or expected.<br /> <br /> It's about these Changelings having very limited time to spend in the mortal world. If they are spending six days out of the week at the homestead in the Dreaming, for example, that is not enough time to earn any kind of income that could provide them a place of business, a rent or mortgage, enough time to sell goods or services, etc. Even yoga instructors, massage therapists, New Age shop sellers, tourist trap managers, reiki practitioners, etc. will be working around a full work week in the mortal world.<br /> <br /> The moment you starting saying these Changelings are spending enough time in the mortal world to allow them to run businesses, pay rent, utilities, taxes, etc. then those Changelings aren't spending any real time in the homestead.<br /> <br /> To me, living in a homestead implies that any Changelings choosing to live there are spending most of their time in the Dreaming. They don't have an immediate access to the Autumn World like normal freeholds. They must first travel to other Freeholds or kinds of Trods simply to get to the Autumn World. Choosing to reside in a homestead implies they want to spend most of their time in the Dreaming. If they wanted to spend so much time in the Autumn World, they'd be using some other kind of Freehold type. As such they have minimal ties to the Autumn World. They need some kind of mortal concept that enables them to meet the minimal requirements to ward off Bedlam despite the limited time they have to spend there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T21:43:19-07:00","id":1492413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492407#post1492407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling has one big problem in that most pre-20 supplements have a visible problem of leaning so much in one aspect of the game the author liked as to effectively ignore and contradict lore of other aspects, at least to a degree. Most of the time it isn't a big problem, but it does means some inconsistencies have to be accounted for to understand a given element of the supplements. Homesteads fit this bill. Their original depiction completely ignores that Changelings aren't the original state of the Kithain and that Bedlam exists for them, so they work as Dreaming Freeholds that were cut from the Autumn World during the Interregnum and now conflict ensues, and their inhabitants are completely normal Changelings just 'cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That is exactly the issue. Given the other constraints we have, how do Changelings residing in homesteads make everything work. Bedlam being the real constraint here.<br /> <br /> Do such changelings homesteaders work this out themselves? Do most homesteads rely on alliances with other motleys who do spend most of their time in the Autumn World to piggy back on their efforts? If so, what do they provide in exchange? Do some rely on controlling in some way certain knowing Kinain, enchanted mortals, etc. to provide that benefit? If so, how do the homesteaders maintain this relationship?<br /> <br /> I think there are lots of different answers. And while certain types of solutions may seem to be more likely than others, specific scenarios can make a lot of concepts work in practice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T04:59:46-07:00","id":1492424,"title":"","content":"Jumping off from a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488496-fairy-stocks-fetches\">previous conversation</a>, I would say that the need for a little Banality to stave off Bedlam would be a good incentive to take enchanted mortals into the Dreaming. A homestead still needs someone to cook, clean, feed the hippogriff, etc. And that sort of tedious activity, even in fantastic scenery, is tedious, and Banal. These &quot;banality batteries&quot; eventually fall to Bedlam if they aren't eaten or carried off by something dreadful, and need replacements.<br /> <br /> In my home campaigns, Hearts Realms (Echoes of Arcadia) and Otherworlds (Aetherial Realms, Shard Realms, Horizon Realms, etc) count as the &quot;real world&quot; for the sake of staving off Bedlam. However, these places have their own rules and rulers, so should be approached with caution. Such places include; Capecia, the Hollow Earth, Mount Olympus, Niflheim and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-06-2022, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T09:51:16-07:00","id":1492435,"title":"","content":"I'd have to check the older book but, I believe that homesteads are often linked to other freeholds. The Homestead being the country side to the Court. So the changelings that live in the homestead would travel to the court in question and socialize with their cousins there, kind of like when your rich snooty relatives come down for a holiday to rub in your nose how much better they have it then you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T10:04:11-07:00","id":1492436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492424#post1492424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jumping off from a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488496-fairy-stocks-fetches\">previous conversation</a>, I would say that the need for a little Banality to stave off Bedlam would be a good incentive to take enchanted mortals into the Dreaming. A homestead still needs someone to cook, clean, feed the hippogriff, etc. And that sort of tedious activity, even in fantastic scenery, is tedious, and Banal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't even considered the possibility that mortals taken into the Dreaming could provide some of the ties to stave off Banality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N0uHSEtOCSM\" data-code=\"N0uHSEtOCSM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/N0uHSEtOCSM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I'm reluctant to say that it eliminates the need to enter the Autumn World on a regular basis, but it could qualify for meeting some requirements of having ties to mortals and thus contribute. It would also explain why fae of either court might engage in that kind of kidnapping. If having that mortal servant in your freehold does contribute in some way to fending off Bedlam, it creates an incentive for Changeling characters to act more like actual fairy characters.<br /> <br /> It does seem like a big cheat to the rules as intended. But since it contributes to making the setting seem more like actual fairy lore (rather than making the setting less like its inspirations), I am much more inclined to go with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492424#post1492424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These &quot;banality batteries&quot; eventually fall to Bedlam if they aren't eaten or carried off by something dreadful, and need replacements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think technically mortals in the Dreaming succumb to becoming &quot;Dreamstruck&quot;, not &quot;Bedlam&quot;, but the two effects are very similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T10:41:33-07:00","id":1492438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm reluctant to say that it eliminates the need to enter the Autumn World on a regular basis, but it could qualify for meeting some requirements of having ties to mortals and thus contribute. It would also explain why fae of either court might engage in that kind of kidnapping. If having that mortal servant in your freehold does contribute in some way to fending off Bedlam, it creates an incentive for Changeling characters to act more like actual fairy characters. </div> </div> </div>Maybe not eliminate. But certainly diminish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492436#post1492436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem like a big cheat to the rules as intended. But since it contributes to making the setting seem more like actual fairy lore (rather than making the setting less like its inspirations), I am much more inclined to go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really a cheat but an act of diminished humanity. Changeling who take this path are sacrificing mortals for their own stability. I would even go so far as to have soul collecting Nightmare creatures coming around to carry off Dream-struck mortals much like the legendary tithe to &quot;Hell&quot;. In my home settings, classic horned and hoofed demons, tentacled horrors and the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aslynthi\" target=\"_blank\">Aslynthi </a>often fill this role.<br /> <br /> Another means by which a homesteader might fend off Banality would be to take part in seasonal rituals and holidays. Such rituals have very complex rules in folklore (with even a minor seeming faux pas being quite deadly), but are often tedious, rigid and a bit Banal. In my head canon, the fae made an ancient pact with the Weaver in order to bind the Fomorians (eliminating a serious threat to the pattern web). This deal with Stasis involves strict rituals and taboos that have been largely neglected, but are dangerous to fae practitioners due to its flirtation with Weaver spirits.<br /> <br /> So all of this can go together quite well, but enters into dark territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-06-2022, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T16:57:28-07:00","id":1492465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492424#post1492424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A homestead still needs someone to cook, clean, feed the hippogriff, etc. And that sort of tedious activity, even in fantastic scenery, is tedious, and Banal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say this kind of work is Banal just because it is tedious. You can still create wonder through a well done tedious work.<br /> <br /> And that would actually contradict the lore as one of the Boggan Birthrights is precisely to do this kind of tedious stuff. Also, it can be done by Chimera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492436#post1492436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem like a big cheat to the rules as intended. But since it contributes to making the setting seem more like actual fairy lore (rather than making the setting less like its inspirations), I am much more inclined to go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure that it would go against the spirit of the rules. Using mortals in the Dreaming to keep Bedlam at bay does give an incentive for a behavior even the game recognizes as common, and would justify a lot of concepts while not really ignoring the theme.<br /> <br /> What it may have as a balance to it is the risk of causing the opposite effect if the Changeling doesn't take care. I'd say it helps when the mortal brought helps you remember the Autumn World and its good sides, and keeps you thinking of their needs and safety, so you're not going full nuts just because you're in the Dreaming. On the other side, losing such 'guests' to the ravages of the Dreaming may bring some or all of the avoided Nightmare crashing back to you, or even more if you become too inured to such happenstances.<br /> <br /> Keeping always in mind: Banality isn't the same as the Autumn World even when there is a connection. In fact, the most well known treatment for Imbalance and Bedlam involves cutting yourself for a time from all things Fae, but having a positive experience within the Autumn World, something some Changelings don't even believe possible, but many normal people have regularly. The experience isn't Banal, it just doesn't need Glamour to be enjoyable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T18:35:47-07:00","id":1492472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492465#post1492465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say this kind of work is Banal just because it is tedious. You can still create wonder through a well done tedious work.<br /> <br /> And that would actually contradict the lore as one of the Boggan Birthrights is precisely to do this kind of tedious stuff. Also, it can be done by Chimera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Against the lore for Boggans perhaps. But that is a particular aspect of that kith. However I take your point. Many wonderful things come from long work, study and tedium. <br /> <br /> So I agree that the banality of enchanted mortals remind fae of their mortal existence, as you mention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T21:44:29-07:00","id":1492479,"title":"","content":"I think that is just a discussion on how personal tastes differ and how some work can be tedious and soul destroying for some, while for others the same work can be fulfilling and creates pride. The best we can say is that certain kind of tasks are more likely to be Banal than others.<br /> <br /> After reading the Enchanted book again, I see that enchanted mortals with high Banality better avoid the state of Dreamstruck. So homesteaders would do best by abducting mortals with naturally high Banality and assign them to Banal tasks if they are to last a long time in the Dreaming. That avoids them getting hit with Dreamstruck and possibly losing them. At the same time, since mortals at Banality 8 or higher are uncomfortable to be around, it can't be too high. One can argue the effects of fairy kidnapping on such high Banal people, but you don't want Autumn People as your servants in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> At the same time, any Changelings there would need to establish real relations with them if their presence is to help in fending off Bedlam for the Changelings. So this isn't likely to be chattel slavery where the owners have a superficial relationship with their slaves. It could be a wicked step-sisters/step-mother relationship, but still something familiar and often intimate rather than business-like. Such mortal servants should be more like family and close friends rather than distant coworkers. But their status as mortals, not beings of the Dreaming, would be paramount.<br /> <br /> I wonder if instead of random people, it would be better for the Changelings to select mortals from the same family line or some other connection mortals would recognize. That would cement their ties not just to individual mortals, but to the <i>mortal world</i>. For humans, it might be seen as some form of family curse that family members seem to go mad or disappear every generation or a few generations. Or something tied to inhabitants of the same land, even if families come and go down the centuries. As long as it establishes a connection between fae and mortal, it'd be good.<br /> <br /> I still think homesteaders would still need to travel to the Autumn World at some point every year, but such enchanted mortal servants would alleviate a lot of the burden. That makes me wonder if homesteads should be known for having a high number of enchanted mortal servants/slaves compared to other freeholds. Of course, such enchanted mortals might be treated better than just slaves - we discussed that in the other thread - but the point persists. Such an arrangement might even be necessary for many homesteads to simply survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T21:49:04-07:00","id":1492480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492435#post1492435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to check the older book but, I believe that homesteads are often linked to other freeholds. The Homestead being the country side to the Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that can be a good analogy. But I wonder how many times it might be the other way around. Might homesteads be more prestigious than other Freeholds, simply because they are more part of the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> It would require any nobles who live there to visit other places and not have others come to them, but &quot;trooping fairies&quot; are an established part of fairy lore. This might be a good explanation for it.<br /> <br /> I think homesteads are probably a bad option for PCs because most STs and players will want heavy involvement in the mortal world. But an ST isn't bound by that when presenting the NPCs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T02:55:41-07:00","id":1492497,"title":"","content":"I agree that it wouldn't completely free homesteaders from having to travel to the Autumn World, but easing the burden from once a week to once a year for basic survival would help in broadening possible concepts a lot. Specially because it is far easier to have many of them doing such trips more frequently than needed if that fits your idea, just because they don't need to do it to stave off Bedlam doesn't mean they don't need to do it for other reasons of their own or just because they want. On the other hand, having those who would stay too long in your stories degenerate too fast is a burden. In a common Freehold one week is plenty of time, in a Homestead, not at all.<br /> <br /> Keeping humans in the Dreaming may have other consequences, too, that Homesteaders would have to account for. Freeholds usually don't have permanent human residents, just temporary &quot;guests&quot; for parties and short stays. While even in C20 there are no hard rules on this, more than one book references the risk of the Dreaming being tainted by Banality. There are even rare things like Banal Chimeras and Cold-Iron Treasures that combine the powers of the Dreaming with Banality, sometimes with explosive effects (one such a Treasure is literally explosive, like, it is a cross that when activated by an Autumn Person against fae goes boom with demolition-level intensity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T04:15:21-07:00","id":1492501,"title":"","content":"I think all of this could be tied to or invigorated by the old seasonal cycles of the fae. There are times when the Dreaming and the Autumn World are closer, and times when they are not. The concept of the fae being creatures of a place also comes into it. Faerie glens, wells, rivers etc, being part of the link to a homestead. Refitted to the modern world, this could be things like haunted highways, free hot dog day at Wrigley Field or when a mega millions jackpot is particularly high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T05:58:45-07:00","id":1492510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492480#post1492480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that can be a good analogy. But I wonder how many times it might be the other way around. Might homesteads be more prestigious than other Freeholds, simply because they are more part of the Dreaming?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no I definitely agree. This isn't &quot;redneck country side&quot;, if you excuse the term, this is &quot;Mansions on 100 acres&quot; country side. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492480#post1492480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think homesteads are probably a bad option for PCs because most STs and players will want heavy involvement in the mortal world. But an ST isn't bound by that when presenting the NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that any chronicle that takes place more in the Dreaming than the Autumn world tends to lose part of the identity of what makes the Splat fun to play. But Like I said, I'd probably have some sort of &quot;Beverly Hills&quot; homestead to the &quot;LA&quot; court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T13:24:46-07:00","id":1492552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492501#post1492501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all of this could be tied to or invigorated by the old seasonal cycles of the fae. There are times when the Dreaming and the Autumn World are closer, and times when they are not. The concept of the fae being creatures of a place also comes into it. Faerie glens, wells, rivers etc, being part of the link to a homestead. Refitted to the modern world, this could be things like haunted highways, free hot dog day at Wrigley Field or when a mega millions jackpot is particularly high.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine this can be easily simulated by simply having certain Trods open and close at different times of the day, week, or year, or when certain events take place (a comet appears, a falling star is sighted, when a human enters a certain spot, when a thunderstorm happens, or... free hot dog day at Wrigley Field).<br /> <br /> So a homestead might be the crossroads of a certain number of trods. But most of those trods leading to the mortal world are closed most of the time. But this trod opens up during the spring equinox, and this one opens up during the winter solstice, and this one opens during free hot dog day, etc. And during those times, the homesteaders leave and explore/interact with the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> Trods tied to certain events/times in the mortal world would be an interesting way to create a connection to the Autumn World for those homesteading Changelings. It's not an obvious connection like having specific mortal people you have a relationship with, but it does end up being an important one to the world itself. If the changelings somehow make themselves important on the mortal side when these trods open (they affect mortals in some way, and this is noticed and becomes part of the folklore of the area), it's some justification for how they can avoid Bedlam.<br /> <br /> That way you can do very specific things like have all the homesteaders play ninepins in the Adirondack mountains when there is a bad thunderstorm brewing. Or local legends of a &quot;spirit&quot; haunting the area every Halloween and the like. Instead of these being random events that are hard to justify always happening, it instead becomes important to the operation of a homestead because such anniversary activities are important rituals for those Changelings to avoid Bedlam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T13:36:55-07:00","id":1492554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492313-homesteads-freehold-type?p=1492497#post1492497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping humans in the Dreaming may have other consequences, too, that Homesteaders would have to account for. Freeholds usually don't have permanent human residents, just temporary &quot;guests&quot; for parties and shows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading about the Cow People and the Pig People. They were human groups that lived permanently in the Dreaming. The animal reference is about preferred livestock. The Cow People generally having descended from 19th immigrants to the Dreaming and the Pig People being hippies that immigrated during and after the 1960s. <br /> <br /> These groups were described in the same book as the effects of the Far Dreaming and Deep Dreaming on Changelings. It also introduced the Adhene, if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> So Humans can and do live in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Thought, if a Freehold maintains a cover, like my proposed ones, them the Residents of Homesteads associated with that Freehold could do temp work at that cover. This would let them cover certain practical needs or goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-07-2022, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}